Still another approach with somewhat different semantics is

{.i ko zukte lo ka ce'u pinxe lo ladru kei lo nu do binxo lo ka tsali}

Here you are insisting that they drink their milk and also that they have
the act of becoming strong as a goal in drinking their milk.

mi'e la latro'a mu'o

On Wed, Nov 12, 2014 at 3:37 PM, Ian Johnson <blindbravado@gmail.com> wrote:

> A rather verbose approach which avoids the issue of {ko} scope entirely:
>
> .i mi minde do lo ka ce'u pinxe lo ladru kei mu'i lo nu mi djica lo nu do
> binxo lo ka tsali [kei kei noi lo nu pinxe cu rinka ke'a]
>
> mi'e la latro'a mu'o
>

